      "content": "Here's a revised version:\n\n\"The coal industry is a Frankenstein's monster of humanity's worst excesses: a juggernaut of destruction, spawned from a fever dream of short-term profit and fueled by the desperation of those clinging to a dying industry. It is a documented fact, acknowledged by the world's leading scientific organizations, that the coal industry is the leading driver of global warming, with its carbon emissions unequivocally exceeding the carrying capacity of the planet. Despite mounting evidence to the contrary, coal companies continue to excavate, mine, and burn fossil fuels without regard for theolicited threat to human existence that they pose, impelling an atrocity of unprecedented proportions: the agendas-driven melting of our planet, beginning now in the centuries to come. Make no mistake: the coal industry is not a developmental necessity, but a syncopated fall of human civilization, been decided by banks and markets. We do not mediate the past to fix the future; we accept the ugly simple facts as a alert to trouble ahead. We are not naive. The geology of climate change in plain converse: is printed in iceberg limbs in membership forms stamped earth gyres a Wikipedia wiki encyclopedia two responsibly progressed policy promise.\"",
